<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27147" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lūdī^brĭōsus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		ludibrium, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of mockery</i> or <i>scorn,
				mocking, scornful</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">probra ludibriosa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					7, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auspicia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 15, 5, 25</span></i>
			.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lūdī^brĭosē</span></b> , <i>scornfully</i>, <i><span class="en">Amm. 26,
			6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tert. Res. Carn. 61</span></i>.</div>
